"""Write the lead's bounded physical verdicts from audited per-target evidence."""
import csv,json,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;W=B.parent
Q=list(csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(newline='',encoding='utf8')))
G={x['tic']:x for x in json.loads((B/'lead-gaia-covariance.json').read_text())}
C={x['tic']:x for x in json.loads((B/'lead-current-sectors.json').read_text())}
N=json.loads((W/'shared-catalogues/gaia-neighbors.json').read_text())['targets']
R={
'T031':('REFUTED','The s25 millimagnitude fluctuations near 1985.45, 2006.53 and 2007.55 sit in an irregular, gently varying raw baseline; their shallow few-point troughs do not have stable isolated ingress/egress and two are only 1.02 d apart. The larger s86 selected windows lie on a pronounced ramp, step and an interrupted baseline, with no return to a stable local level. The actual raw shapes and discontinuities positively refute these selected eclipse flags; incompatible spacings are supporting context, not a blanket exclusion of other eclipses.','No secure isolated eclipse center or period can be measured from these flags.','Reopen if a clean isolated same-kind event appears in future data.'),
'T032':('REFUTED','The s94 trough around 3875 follows the same spacecraft-orbit gap morphology as independent targets T035, T038 and T039, with a 0.25 d local gap. The s101 and s102 candidate minima terminate and begin at 1.71 and 1.89 d missing intervals; s104 is another broad baseline/gap variation. Their spacings do not form one 48.47 d same-kind clock. This is positive gap and raw-shape evidence against the selected eclipses.','All four retained windows are interrupted or broad; none supports a measured center.','Reassess only with a fully observed isolated return to baseline.'),
'T033':('PLAUSIBLE','s80 contains a coherent roughly 6-8 ppt, roughly 2 d flat-bottomed deficit around BTJD 3501.945. A target-containing TESScut aperture reproduces it. s91 starts in a roughly 1% low state 0.434 d before the Gaia-period predicted center at 3775.870 and recovers over the following day; its target-containing TESScut apertures reproduce the partial occasion. The missing s91 ingress and baseline permit a sector-start reset alternative.','The s80-to-s91 separation is conditional on five Gaia cycles; n=3/4/5 remain untested. s92 flat core coverage contradicts n=6/9 and disfavors n=8 under the assumed phase, duration and depth; n=8 has only partial core coverage (424 cadences, first offset -0.383 d for a +/-0.6 d core), n=7 falls in a gap, and n=10 is at a sector-start low state. The s80 WCS target has flux, but nearby sources remain a source-attribution limit.','Capture a fully bracketed repeat in a future sector and resolve the 18.8 arcsec G=14.89 neighbor with event difference imaging or higher-resolution photometry.'),
'T034':('REFUTED','The s81 raw aperture divides into two widely separated flux branches throughout the selected window, and the full sector shows a large decline, gap and recovery. Its 0.06 d candidate dip is a few points on the changing upper branch while the lower branch persists outside it. That pattern is positive extraction/contamination evidence against an isolated eclipse.','No unique astrophysical deficit or timing center is supported.','A future clean aperture could test for independent periodic dips.'),
'T035':('REFUTED','The s94 broad trough around 3874.6 is accompanied by a 0.25 d spacecraft gap and long raw baseline drift. The same s94 depression appears at nearly the same time in T032, T038 and T039, which have different sky positions and Gaia periods. The common timing is supporting context; the actual broad raw shape and gap supply the contrary evidence.','Only one disrupted window exists; no measured eclipse clock.','Revisit an isolated event away from the spacecraft gap.'),
'T036':('PLAUSIBLE','s85 has an approximately 12 ppt broad depression around 3625.1 with an extended low interval and recovery. Other s85 troughs near 3611, 3617 and 3630 differ in shape, and several lie beside gaps; their 5-14 d intervals do not establish same-kind 54.23 d eclipses. The main broad event remains an insecure eclipse interpretation, so the other troughs do not justify refuting all astrophysical dips.','One sector contains several broad changing-baseline troughs but no supported Gaia-period timing or secure repeat. The quick TESScut has a cropped zero-valued half; its aperture statistic is invalid and cannot act as an independent null or source localization.','Obtain a fully bracketed same-kind return and a valid spatial difference image with a stable local baseline.'),
'T037':('REFUTED','The s73 SAP trough near 3300.9 begins after a 0.35 d gap with a roughly -21 ppt raw step. A target-containing TESScut 3x3 and 5x5 background-subtracted extraction lacks the QLP trough while the cutout background changes broadly. Together these spatial and gap facts positively support a background/extraction disturbance in the selected window; corrected-flux suppression alone is not the argument.','The local TESSCut background estimate is approximate, so the spatial test alone cannot exclude every physical signal; combined with the coincident gap/step, this selected trough does not support a target eclipse or clock.','Test any future isolated raw target-aperture event away from a background transition.'),
'T038':('REFUTED','The sole s94 candidate is the same broad, gap-adjacent ~3875 depression seen in several unrelated s94 targets. Its raw trough extends across a 0.25 d gap and lacks an isolated stable baseline; no second event follows the 57.16 d Gaia orbit. The actual gap/shape supports a spacecraft-origin false flag.','One disrupted window only; no reliable eclipse center.','Seek a clean repeat in a later sector.'),
'T039':('REFUTED','The sole s94 3875.1 trough is broad and interrupted by a 0.25 d gap, matching the timing and morphology of the s94 depression in unrelated T032, T035 and T038. The local raw baseline changes across the window rather than making a stable isolated eclipse.','There is no measured same-kind return at the 50.14 d Gaia period.','Reopen if a future sector shows a fully bracketed event.'),
'T040':('REFUTED','The s29 selected six-point decline occurs on the edge of a large flare-like excursion and before a 3.54 d interruption; it is not an isolated eclipse against a stable baseline. The s96 broad shallow trough occurs beside a 0.22 d gap and sector-scale reset, 1825 d later with no supported same-kind clock. These actual raw shapes positively refute the selected eclipse interpretation.','Neither flagged occasion supports a precise center or physical eclipse depth.','Require an isolated repeat independent of flare or sector boundary.'),
}
fields=['sample_id','tic','sample_stratum','physical_verdict','full_review_completion','novelty_status','period_days','period_error_days','primary_epoch_btjd','depth_ppt','limitations','next_check','report']
rows=[]
for q in Q:
 sid=q['sample_id'];tic=q['tic'];verdict,evidence,limit,nextcheck=R[sid]
 m=json.loads((B/tic/'lead-numeric.json').read_text());g=G[tic];receipt=W/'source-packets'/tic/'sources.json';sp=hashlib.sha256(receipt.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
 ns=[x for x in N[sid] if x['source_id']!=q['gaia_dr3'] and float(x['separation_arcsec'])<25]
 neighbor='; '.join(f"{float(x['separation_arcsec']):.1f} arcsec G={float(x['phot_g_mean_mag']):.2f}" for x in ns[:8]) or 'none within 25 arcsec in the shared Gaia cone'
 if len(ns)>8:neighbor+=f'; plus {len(ns)-8} additional crowded-field rows in the shared cone'
 sectors=', '.join(f"s{x['sector']} [{x['start_btjd']:.2f}, {x['end_btjd']:.2f}]" for x in m['coverage'])
 event_lines='\n'.join(f"- s{e['sector']} screen {e['screen_btjd']:.3f}: raw core deficit {e['raw_core_median_deficit_ppt']:.1f} ppt, side scatter {e['raw_side_scatter_ppt']:.1f} ppt, quality-zero core {e['quality0_core_n']}, local max gap {e['local_max_gap_days']:.3f} d; exploratory fit midpoint {e.get('fit_mid_btjd',float('nan')):.3f}." for e in m['events'])
 if not event_lines:event_lines='- No retained dip flag in available files.'
 closest=g['closest']; sig=closest.get('linear_sigma_days')
 geometry=f"The Gaia DR3 SB1 orbit has P={float(q['gaia_period_days']):.6f} d. At the screening time {g['evaluation_epoch_btjd']:.3f}, the closest edge-on conjunction differs by {closest['offset_days']:.3f} d; linear Gaia covariance gives {sig:.3f} d. This comparison uses a screening time, except where a measured event is separately described, and cannot turn a raw artifact into an eclipse."
 if sid=='T033':geometry+=f" The exploratory fitted s80 midpoint 3501.945 and conditional +5 Gaia cycles predict 3775.870 in s91; see lead-phase.json and lead-aliases.json. This is not a unique photometric period."
 available=C[tic].get('response',{}).get('results',[])
 newest=max((int(x['sectorName'].split('-')[1][1:]) for x in available),default=None)
 maxcache=max(x['sector'] for x in m['coverage'])
 if newest is None:availability='Current MAST footprint query failed; later coverage is unknown.'
 elif newest<=maxcache:availability=f"The current MAST footprint lists sectors through {newest}, no later than cached s{maxcache}."
 else:availability=f"The current MAST footprint lists s{newest} beyond cached s{maxcache}; this review has not treated that sector as a null."
 text=f"# {sid} - TIC {tic}\n\n**Physical verdict:** {verdict}. **Bounded review:** COMPLETE. **Catalogue novelty:** UNKNOWN; four VizieR gates remained unavailable after failed positive controls in the shared catalogue work. The successful scoped primary-table nonmatches do not clear novelty.\n\n## Raw flux, timing, and coverage\n\n{evidence}\n\n{event_lines}\n\nCached QLP raw-SAP spans: {sectors}. Actual finite-cadence and quality-zero counts, endpoints and gaps are in [numeric evidence](lead-numeric.json) and [helper coverage](../helper-coverage.json). Screening times and trapezoid fits are exploratory, not automatically accepted eclipse midpoints. Full-sector and local plots are in this target folder.\n\n## Source, alternative reduction, and Gaia geometry\n\n{geometry}\n\nGaia neighbors within 25 arcsec: {neighbor}. Target positions and all neighbors to 120 arcsec are in the shared Gaia neighbor receipt; flux ratios alone do not localize a dip."
 if sid=='T033':text+=" Terra04's background-subtracted TESScut 3x3/5x5 light curves reproduce the s80 dip and the s91 partial low state with real target flux; both reductions use the same TESS photons. The deficit peaks near the target in coarse pixels; the crowded field prevents a definitive unique-source claim."
 elif sid=='T037':text+=" Terra04's target-containing TESScut extraction and background map provide the deciding alternative reduction and spatial contradiction; see helper pixel receipts and plots."
 elif sid=='T036':text+=" Raw SAP morphology was checked against the available QLP alternate flux where present; no alternative reduction establishes a recurring eclipse. This missing check is retained in the limitation rather than used as refutation."
 else:text+=" An additional pipeline is not required to refute the selected flags where their raw time-series gaps, inconsistent spacings or extraction behavior provide positive contrary evidence."
 text+=f"\n\n{availability} The footprint response is in [current-sector receipt](../lead-current-sectors.json).\n\n## Limit and next check\n\n{limit} {nextcheck}\n\nSource packet SHA-256: `{sp}`. Every QLP FITS read by the numeric script matched the bulk packet SHA-256; paths and hashes are in lead-numeric.json and batch SOURCE-HASHES.json. This is a bounded physical review, not a literature priority claim.\n"
 path=B/tic/'REPORT.md';path.write_text(text,encoding='utf8')
 rows.append(dict(sample_id=sid,tic=tic,sample_stratum=q['sample_stratum'],physical_verdict=verdict,full_review_completion='COMPLETE',novelty_status='UNKNOWN',period_days='',period_error_days='',primary_epoch_btjd='',depth_ppt='6.5' if sid=='T033' else '',limitations=limit,next_check=nextcheck,report=str(path)))
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf8') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
print([(x['sample_id'],x['physical_verdict']) for x in rows])
